{"name":"Dolly Cheek","hex":"#fcc9b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dolly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A doll.","A roughly cylindrical wooden object used as a base when molding pie crust."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit a dolly.","To move (an object) using a dolly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dolly"},{"term":"cheek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft skin on each side of the face, below the eyes; the outer surface of the sides of the oral cavity.","The lower part of the buttocks that is often exposed beneath very brief underwear, swimwear, or extremely short shorts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be impudent towards.","To pull a horse's head back toward the saddle using the cheek strap of the bridle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheek","blocks":[{"text":"The cheeks constitute the area of the face below the eyes and between the nose and the left or right ear. Buccal means relating to the cheek. In humans, the region is innervated by the buccal nerve. The area between the inside of the cheek and the teeth and gums is called the vestibule or buccal pouch or buccal cavity and forms part of the mouth. In other animals, the cheeks may also be referred to as \"jowls\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Cheek.jpg/330px-Cheek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheek"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/1280px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_